temp/
*.out
*.test
coverage.out
*.exe
# The two build/ exes are committed on purpose: they are this product's own release output and the
# winget/MSIX manifests point a clone at them without a local Go toolchain.
!build/*.exe
# pdftotext and its three MinGW runtime DLLs are a vendored upstream binary (Poppler), not build
# output - the converter shells out to them and they ship inside every package.
!internal/bundledtools/pdftotext/*.dll
# Extracted EPUB directories in test_epub
test_epub/
test_pdf/
test_txt/
# Local sample documents used by the integration tests (tests/testdoc_test.go).
# The files are private and must never be committed; the tests skip when absent.
test_doc/
# The OCR visual-fidelity corpus lives under test_doc/ and is therefore already ignored - this
# line is here so the rule is findable from the lab's own docs. Only the metadata is committed
# (DEV/ocrlab/corpus.json + annotations); the media is third-party work and ships in nothing.
test_doc/ocrlab/
DEV/private/
# Spec/plan tickets are working notes, not part of the shipped repo - they stay local.
DEV/plan/
# Secrets and signing material - pre-empt the leak, never catch it afterwards.
*.pfx
*.snk
*.jks
*.keystore
.env
*token*
*secret*
